  "geometry_notes": "World box: axis-aligned wireframe cube spanning x,y,z ∈ [-3,3] (edge 6 units), drawn as thin lines in light blue #5B9BD5 at ~1px. Axes are black lines through the origin extending to ±3.2 with small perpendicular tick marks every 0.5 unit; +x points toward screen lower-left, +y toward screen lower-right, +z straight up (standard isometric axonometric pose). Labels: italic 'x' at the lower-left end of the x-axis, italic 'y' at the lower-right end of the y-axis, 'z' at the top of the z-axis with an arrowhead.\n\nTube S: a tube of radius 0.35 swept along an open space curve that winds back on itself, e.g. r(t) = (1.9 cos t, 1.7 sin 2t, 0.55 sin t) for t ∈ [0.15, 2π+0.6] — the resulting shape has two lobes, one sweeping behind/above the z-axis toward the upper right of the frame and one sweeping in front/below toward the lower right, with the strands crossing near the z-axis so the tube visibly overlaps itself in the chosen view. Tube color blue-gray #6E7CA3 with lighter specular highlight #9AA6C4 and slightly darker interior wall #55618A; render double-sided so the open ends show inner wall.\nOpen far mouth: circular disc of radius 0.35 at the tube's far end, positioned in the upper-right region of the box (roughly x≈1.2, y≈1.8, z≈0.9), its plane roughly perpendicular to the tube axis so it reads as a tilted ellipse.\nBoundary circle C: the near end of the tube, radius 0.35, centered just right of and slightly below the origin (roughly x≈0.1, y≈-0.2, z≈-0.35), its plane facing the viewer so it reads as a near-circular ellipse. Draw its rim as a thicker outlined ring.\nLabels: 'S' in black ~0.3 units above-right of the upper-right lobe (near x≈1.1, y≈2.2, z≈1.3); 'C' in black just above-left of the front opening (near x≈-0.15, y≈-0.2, z≈0.15).\n\nVector field: F(x,y,z) = (1 + 0.25 z², 1, 0.4 + 0.4 z). Sampled on a 4×4×4 grid over [-2.5,2.5]³ plus extra samples placed on the tube surface. All arrows drawn at a fixed length ≈0.45 units (direction only, as in the source), orange #E8622A, cone head ~0.15 long. Because Fz grows with z and the horizontal components stay fixed, the arrows visibly tilt up and to the right more steeply near the top of the box — match that trend.\nCurl mode: curl F = (0, 0.5 z, 0), drawn in a distinct warm color (#C0392B) with length proportional to |0.5 z| (clamped 0.15–0.5) so the arrows vanish near z=0 and lengthen toward the top and bottom; outward unit normals n on the tube drawn as short gray-green (#4C8C6B) arrows of length 0.35 at the same surface sample points, so the learner can compare curl F direction against n.\nBoundary-emphasis mode: tube opacity drops to ~0.15, circle C rim drawn thick in #E8622A/gold with 6 small tangent arrowheads spaced around it showing counterclockwise orientation as seen from the viewer (consistent with the outward normal by the right-hand rule).",
  "notes": "Build the tube with THREE.TubeGeometry on a CatmullRomCurve3 (or a Curve subclass evaluating the parametric formula), tubularSegments ≈ 400, radialSegments 24, closed:false, MeshStandardMaterial(side: DoubleSide, roughness 0.5, metalness 0.05) plus a hemisphere light and one directional key light from upper-left. Cap/ring meshes (THREE.CircleGeometry + torus rim) at both ends for the open mouths. Arrows as instanced cone+cylinder meshes or a pool of THREE.ArrowHelper reused between modes so toggling only updates directions/colors, not geometry counts. Wireframe box from THREE.LineSegments on BoxGeometry edges; ticks as tiny LineSegments. Labels ('x','y','z','S','C') as CSS2DRenderer sprites that always face the camera and stay legible during orbit. Use an orthographic camera in an isometric pose to match the axonometric look; OrbitControls with damping, no zoom past the box. Depth-sort correctly for the self-overlapping tube (depthWrite true, no transparency in default mode); when fading the tube for boundary emphasis, enable transparency and set depthWrite false so field arrows behind it remain visible."
}

